  "id": "DrugBank_DB00352 - MONDO_18435",
  "verbalization": "Tioguanine shows a strong association with Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) through multiple indirect pathways, suggesting a potential role in the pathogenesis of this disease. The evidence indicates that Tioguanine is linked to AML via the drug Idarubicin, which in turn is associated with AML with the specific chromosomal abnormality Inv3(p21;q26.2) or T(3;3)(p21;q26.2). This suggests that Tioguanine may influence AML progression through a mechanism that involves Idarubicin, potentially by modulating cellular processes that are dysregulated in this leukemia subtype. The presence of multiple indirect pathways, including the involvement of Idarubicin, supports a mechanistic link between Tioguanine and AML, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence is consistent with a role in AML pathogenesis, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct mechanism of action.",
